Content:
Canadian here;
I can only recall having sloppy joes maybe 2-3 times in my life. They were not a staple of the school cafeteria when and where I was in school in the 90s.

Not going to lie, I don't really understand the appeal of them. Then again, the middle school cafeteria was loaded with hamburgers, mac and cheese. tater tots, huge muffins, spaghetti etc. and most of that food just plain sucked. High school cafeteria got better, there were salads, breakfast sandwiches that were actually really good, half-decent pasts dishes etc. The food sciences classes had to help in the cafeteria so the menus always had something different every week.
